name: the census
after: 18-xargs
intro: Four commands minimum from here. Build the pipeline one stage at a time
intro: and read the output of each before you add the next -- that is the actual
intro: skill, not memorising flags.
---
setup: Every ref file lists its flags on indented lines beginning with a dash.
setup: A character class avoids having to type a literal tab.
q: count the documented flags in ref/ls, printing only the number
a: grep -c '^[[:space:]]-' /usr/share/learn/ref/ls
a: grep -cE '^[[:space:]]+-' /usr/share/learn/ref/ls
ref: grep
---
setup: In ls -l output the fifth field is the size in bytes.
q: print the total bytes used by every ref file, summing column 5 with awk
a: ls -l /usr/share/learn/ref | awk '{s+=$5} END {print s}'
ref: awk
---
setup: Every level declares the commands it drills on ref: lines. Difference
setup: the whole corpus down to the unique set of commands the curriculum touches.
q: print every command any level drills, one per line, with no duplicates
a: sed -n 's/^ref: //p' /usr/share/learn/levels/* | sort -u
a: grep -h '^ref: ' /usr/share/learn/levels/* | sed 's/^ref: //' | sort -u
ref: sed
